From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Zhao <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] hw/virtio/virtio-rng: bound each entropy request

virtio_rng_process() asks the backend for as many bytes as the guest's
available buffers hold, up to the rate limit's quota, which defaults to
INT64_MAX bytes per period. The backend g_malloc()s each request, so a
guest that posts a 4 GiB buffer makes QEMU allocate 4 GiB, and an
rng-random backend then reads the source into all of it.

Ask for at most 64 KiB at a time. chr_read() already fills the guest's
buffers with what it gets, pushing each with the length written, and
calls virtio_rng_process() again while buffers remain, so a large
buffer is returned partly filled and nothing is left waiting. Linux
asks for 64 bytes per call and the Windows driver uses 4 KiB buffers
on an 8-entry queue, so well-behaved guests never reach the bound.

Upstream's 70074cc48f45 ("backends/rng: cap request size to avoid
oversized allocation") caps the same size inside the backend.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-rng.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-rng.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-rng.c
index 3df5d257..c204816a 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-rng.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-rng.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include "qemu/iov.h"
 #include "qemu/module.h"
 #include "qemu/timer.h"
+#include "qemu/units.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio.h"
 #include "hw/qdev-properties.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-rng.h"
@@ -22,6 +23,12 @@
 #include "qom/object_interfaces.h"
 #include "trace.h"
 
+/*
+ * Guests ask for far less: Linux reads 64 bytes at a time, and the Windows
+ * driver posts 4 KiB buffers on an 8-entry queue (32 KiB).
+ */
+#define VIRTIO_RNG_MAX_REQUEST (64 * KiB)
+
 static bool is_guest_ready(VirtIORNG *vrng)
 {
     VirtIODevice *vdev = VIRTIO_DEVICE(vrng);
@@ -117,6 +124,12 @@ static void virtio_rng_process(VirtIORNG *vrng)
     trace_virtio_rng_request(vrng, size, quota);
 
     size = MIN(vrng->quota_remaining, size);
+    /*
+     * The guest sets the buffer sizes. The backend allocates the request,
+     * so ask for a bounded amount; chr_read() fills what it gets and asks
+     * again while buffers remain.
+     */
+    size = MIN(size, VIRTIO_RNG_MAX_REQUEST);
     if (size) {
         rng_backend_request_entropy(vrng->rng, size, chr_read, vrng);
     }
